            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sunshine"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I just made this for dinner this evening. I have been making it for years. I find it easier to use the refrigerated minced garlic because I always keep a jar in the fridge. I just toss some in the skillet and saulte it in the butter and some olive oil then add the spinach. When the garlic gets a tad brown, it is crunchy and yummy."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ms Jean"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Reminds me of something you would get at a fine Italian restaurant. I halved the recipe because I had one bag of baby spinach. I cooked the spinach for about 3 min, added minced garlic and continued to cook another 2 min (total of 5 min cooking time for spinach works best for me). I need to go a little lighter on the lemon juice (don't want such a prominent lemon taste....too tart). I topped with sea salt and cracked black pepper. UPDATE 10/3/19: Changed things to suit my taste. Skipped the lemon juice. Sauteed onion in EVOO and butter for 5 min, then added the garlic for a min. Added the baby spinach, sauteed 4-5 min. Salt, pepper and topped with feta cheese. (I know, different recipe now.) Nice one-bowl dinner. The modifications brought this to over-the-top deliciousness!",
            "datePublished": "2016-01-06T14:36:44.093Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "HNY BNY"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great “base” recipe! The possibilities are endless for this recipe. I added some smoked paprika, chili powder, mineral salt, pepper, and Parmesan cheese. A-Mazing! Very easily could omit the butter for sautéing to keep it dairy free. Don’t rush your garlic. Let it get a nice golden brown before throwing in the spinach. It’s so worth it in the final product. Super easy and fast to fix.",
            "datePublished": "2021-08-04T00:54:41.477Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "suzyN"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Instead of butter and garlic salt, I used a quality virgin olive oil, crushed the garlic, and a tiny pinch of red pepper flakes then added spinach. Salt and cracked pepper to taste before serving.",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-03T17:22:32.063Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
