            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "bcforssell"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I just made this today for my lunch using the recipe provided. However, I used fresh picked rainbow chard from my garden. I used the stems, cutting them small, as well as the leaves and cooked until the stems still had a little crunch. It was delicious and is now part of my diabetic diet. The flavor is easily changed by adding a little sesame oil or parmesan or feta cheese - options are many according to taste preference.",
            "datePublished": "2016-05-20T19:56:51.413Z"
